    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Bavaria was a duchy from c. 555 to 1623, ruled in turn by the Agilolfings, Frankish kings, Luitpoldings, Welfs and Wittelsbachs.</li><li>Bavarian settlers and the church of Salzburg spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#christianity">Christianity</a> and German speech into the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#alps">Alps</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#austria">Austria</a>.</li><li>Under Maximilian I it led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#catholic-league">Catholic League</a> and in 1623 was raised to an electorate, later the Kingdom of Bavaria.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#austria">Austria</a> began as an eastern frontier march of Bavaria and only became a separate duchy in 1156; Bavarian dialects are still spoken across most of Austria.</p></aside>
    </section>

